abstract: >-
  Plans tool-using agents in which every call is proven well-typed. Each MCP tool contract,
  its JSON Schema input and output, is read through valgebra-planning's contract reader on
  valgebra-jsonschema into sets valgebra decides inclusion and emptiness over; the Boolean
  algebra those sets generate is cut into finitely many cells, and a planner searches the cells
  for a program of tool calls and static type tests on values that reaches the goal whatever
  values inside their output schemas the tools return. valgebra-planning's verifier asks
  valgebra alone, without the cells or the search, about every link of a program, one written
  elsewhere included: each is proven, refuted with a value outside it, or left undecided.
  Studies run this planner and valgebra-planning's on the same tasks, read the contracts of the
  seven MCP reference servers, and measure each cell rule against valgebra-planning's cut.
  Every published count is reproduced by a committed command.
repository-code: "https://github.com/ppigazzini/valplan"
keywords:
  - semantic subtyping
  - JSON Schema
  - predicate abstraction
  - planning under nondeterminism
  - program synthesis
  - tool-using agents
  - Model Context Protocol
